{"more_radio_bootlegger_trunk","caller_joke",7,3650,0,23,1,{"Lyle","My uncle kept an empty fishing rod case in every car","Lyle","Said it explained being out at any hour","June","Did he fish?","Lyle","Couldn't tell a bass from a wet shoe","Lyle","Never put a rod in the case, not once that I saw","Lyle","Deputy asked him what was biting once","June","What'd he say?","Lyle","'The regular ones'","Lyle","Then he asks my uncle where his spot is, now we're in trouble","Lyle","His spot was the liquor store in the next county"}},
{"more_radio_factory_whistle","caller_story_sad",7,3650,0,23,1,{"Roy","I used to set my watch by the plant whistle","June","Was it accurate?","Roy","No, we were all late together","June","Including the boss?","Roy","Boss had the only watch that disagreed","Roy","Funny, that, always HIS watch that was right","Roy","I hear it in my head some mornings - get halfway up before I remember","June","Do you lie back down?","Roy","No, feels like I ought to report somewhere","Roy","Sorry, I started off trying to tell you something funny"}},
{"more_radio_barber_credit","caller_joke",7,3650,0,23,1,{"Lou","A man asked if I'd cut his hair on credit","June","Did you agree?","Lou","Said I'd do the left half now","Lou","He didn't laugh, started asking which half his wife would see first","Lou","He said his left was my right","June","Was it?","Lou","Hell if I know, he kept turning round to show me","June","How did you settle it?","Lou","I cut his hair, he swept up","Lou","He did a better job sweeping than I do, actually - might ask him back"}},
{"more_radio_prison_laundry","caller_story_sad",7,3650,0,23,1,{"Vic","I worked laundry inside","June","For how long?","Vic","Couple of years, why, you want the whole-- it's a laundry story, June","June","Sorry, go on","Vic","It's just laundry, everybody wants the other story","Vic","Anyway - where was I? Towels - yeah","Vic","There was an old guy, always folded his towel before he handed it in","Vic","Really square, too, corners lined up, I'd undo it and chuck it straight in","Vic","Said it wasn't my job to live in his mess","Vic","Only man who ever said anything like that to me in there"}},
{"more_radio_end_of_shift","host",7,3650,18,23,1,{"June","Roy, earlier you said you'd been on your feet since dawn - have you sat down yet?","Roy","Sitting now, didn't know you were checking up on me","June","Well, I'm asking, you sounded worn out","Roy","There's still work","June","There usually is, Roy","Roy","Feels wrong to stop","June","Can somebody else take a turn?","Roy","They offered, I said I was fine","June","Are they still awake? Go ask them again","Roy","Yeah, all right - I'll do that before I get up and find another damn job"}},
{"king_radio_birthday_number","caller_story_sad",7,3650,0,23,1,{"Lena","I think my birthday was last week","June","Happy birthday, Lena","Lena","Don't make a big thing of it","June","All right. A small thing","Lena","I can't remember if I'm thirty-eight or thirty-nine","June","Which would you prefer?","Lena","Thirty-eight. I'd like the extra year","June","Then thirty-eight it is, for this conversation"}},
{"king_radio_telling_time","host",7,3650,0,23,1,{"June","I nearly gave you the time without checking","June","Habit. Say it firmly and it sounds like you know","June","I don't want to get good at that","June","So here's what I can tell you","June","I'm here, and I'm listening when I can","June","Sometimes I need a minute before I answer","June","It doesn't mean I've gone","June","It just means I needed a minute"}},
{"king_radio_cold_appliance","caller_joke",7,3650,0,23,1,{"Frank","Caught myself opening the fridge just to stare into it again","June","Any luck?","Frank","Same as before. I don't know what I expected to grow in there","June","I wouldn't eat it if it did","Frank","That's the first sensible food advice I've had all week","June","Very selective service we're running","Frank","Maybe I'll check a cupboard instead","June","Try to surprise yourself"}},
{"king_radio_parking_ticket","caller_joke",7,3650,0,23,1,{"Vincent","Still got an unpaid parking ticket in my wallet","June","Keeping it as a souvenir?","Vincent","Insurance. First sign of normal life, they'll want sixty dollars","June","You'd pay it?","Vincent","Happily. Then I'd argue about the damn sign for an hour","June","You sound ready","Vincent","Been practicing","June","Save something for the clerk"}},
{"r2_d7_hammer_roster_log","military",7,7,0,23,1,{"Hammer-3-7","Warden Main, Hammer-3-7, request permission to pass a personnel roster for the log, over","Warden Main","Hammer-3-7, is it Category Two personnel or missing personnel, over?","Hammer-3-7","Missing, over","Warden Main","Wait one","Warden Main","Hammer-3-7, send it, last names only, over","Hammer-3-7","Reyes - Tucker - Lindqvist - Sowders - Amos - Delacroix - Whitt - Harlan - Bybee, over","Warden Main","I have nine names - reading back - Reyes, Tucker, Lindqvist, Sowders, Amos, Delacroix, Whitt, Harlan, Bybee, over","Hammer-3-7","Read back correct - Bybee spells it with two Ys, nobody ever gets that right, over","Warden Main","I have it with two Ys, it's in the log, Sergeant - Warden Main, out"}},
{"r2_d7_morning_report_unknown","military",7,9,5,10,1,{"Anvil-7","Anvil-6, Anvil-7 with the morning report, over","Anvil-6","Send it, over","Anvil-7","Assigned, one hundred twelve, present for duty, sixty-one - wounded, four - Category Two, two - killed, nine, missing, thirty-six, over","Anvil-6","Battalion wants the missing split into AWOL and unknown, over","Anvil-7","Sir, I'm carrying all thirty-six as unknown, I won't write AWOL next to a man's name when I don't know where he is, over","Anvil-6","Battalion will kick it back, over","Anvil-7","Then they can kick it back, I'll be right here, over","Anvil-6","Roger, all unknown - Anvil-6, out"}},
{"r2_d7_main_displaces","military",7,8,17,22,1,{"Warden-6","All Warden stations, Warden-6 - Warden Main displaces to Elizabethtown at 2200 tonight - Warden Tac remains at Fort Knox, acknowledge in order, over","Hatchet-6","Hatchet-6, acknowledged - Sir, will the checkpoints still reach Main from Elizabethtown, over?","Warden-6","The retrans site on the hill at Muldraugh relays you - if it goes down, you report to Tac, over","Crowbar-6","Crowbar-6, acknowledged - Sir, is the task force being pulled back behind the checkpoints, over?","Warden-6","The line holds where it is, the headquarters moves, that's all this is, over","Anvil-6","Anvil-6, acknowledged - Sir, my first sergeant asks whether that puts us outside our own quarantine or inside it, over","Warden-6","Tell your first sergeant to clear the net - Warden-6, out"}},
{"r2_d7_red_roof_barns","military",7,9,8,20,1,{"Dustoff 2-2","Mayday, mayday, mayday - Dustoff 2-2, engine failure, going down east of Rosewood, over","Warden Air","Dustoff 2-2, Warden Air - copy mayday - say souls on board, over","Dustoff 2-2","Four souls, two crew, one medic, one patient, picking a field, over","Warden Air","Copy four souls - say grid when able, over","Dustoff 2-2","Grid unknown, north of a white barn with a red roof, south of the water tower, over","Warden Air","Copy white barn, red roof, all aviation this frequency, remain clear - Dustoff 2-2, Warden Air, radio check, over","Bluejay 2-6","Warden Air, Bluejay 2-6, I have smoke south of a water tower east of Rosewood - I'm holding at two thousand feet, over","Warden Air","Bluejay 2-6, maintain two thousand, do not descend - mark it and report, over","Bluejay 2-6","Marked - Warden Air, from up here there are a lot of white barns with red roofs - I'm sorry, over"}},
{"r2_d7_relief_held_at_line","military",7,9,0,23,2,{"Warden Main","Striker-6, Warden Main, relief is confirmed, a battalion from out of state crosses into the county at 0600 tomorrow and relieves your company in place, over","Striker-6","Striker-6, copy relief at 0600, I'll tell them - thank you, over","Striker-6","Warden Main, Striker-6, time is 0930, no relief on the road, over","Warden Main","Striker-6, the relief was held at the county line by order of higher - it won't come today, over","Striker-6","When, over?","Warden Main","No date, units outside the line are not permitted to cross into it - same as everyone else, over","Striker-6","Roger, my soldiers packed their rucks last night, some of them shaved, over","Warden Main","I'm sorry, Striker - Warden Main, out"}},
{"r3_so_d7_one_week","sign_on",7,7,5,8,5,{"Marty","It is Friday, July the sixteenth, one week ago today was an ordinary Friday, I wanted to say that out loud once","Marty","A week ago I sold a man two bags of layer pellets and a salt block, and I told him to have a good weekend","Marty","I've been wondering all morning if he did","Marty","This is ninety-nine point six, March Ridge, I'll be on the air until the generator says otherwise"}},
{"r3_host_d7_white_rags_count","host",7,7,13,21,1,{"Marty","Yesterday I asked anybody listening to tie something white on their mailbox - I drove the main road at noon, a mile each way, and counted","Marty","Nineteen, nineteen mailboxes between the Baptist church and the county garage","Marty","One was a whole bedsheet, one was a pair of boxer shorts, I'm counting the shorts","Marty","There was one more, a little girl's hair ribbon, on the box by the Hensley place - I didn't think anybody was left at the Hensley place","Marty","So that's twenty, twenty of you, on one mile of road, I'll keep talking"}},
{"r7_mil_sitrep_nothing_to_report","military",7,11,5,11,1,{"Cardinal Main","All Cardinal stations, Cardinal Main - morning SITREP, report in order, over","Cardinal-1-6","Cardinal-1-6, no change from yesterday, nothing to report, over","Cardinal Main","1-6, roger","Cardinal-3-6","Cardinal-3-6, nothing to report, over","Cardinal Main","3-6, roger - Cardinal-2-6, send your SITREP, over","Cardinal Main","Cardinal-2-6, Cardinal Main, over","Cardinal-1-6","Main, 1-6, I drove out to 2-6's barrier last night, there's nothing there to report, over","Cardinal Main","1-6, say again, over","Cardinal-1-6","I said there's nothing there, no people, no vehicles, no radio - there's a rifle leaned against the barrier and somebody folded a poncho on the hood, over","Cardinal Main","Roger - Cardinal Main, out"}},
{"r7_ksp_hat_in_the_seat","scanner",7,12,2,7,1,{"Post 4","Trooper 422, Post 4 - radio check","Post 4","422, Post 4, key up for me","Trooper 406","Post 4, 406, I'm at his car - it's at milepost 101 with the lights still going","Post 4","406, go ahead","Trooper 406","Driver's door is open, keys are in it - his hat's on the passenger seat, which he never did in nineteen years, not one time","Post 4","Copy your traffic, 406","Trooper 406","Post 4, do you want me to put out a lookout, or do you want to wait?","Post 4","Put it out, and 406, bring me the hat - don't leave that hat out there in the car"}},
{"r8_hor_shirt_inside_out","caller_story_horror",7,90,21,4,1,{"Arvel","Laundry on a line out on the Ekron road, whole line of it","June","How long had it been there?","Arvel","That's what I'm getting at, it was dry and it was clean, it didn't have that gray on it that stuff gets when it hangs out three weeks","Arvel","Sheets, two pair of overalls, kid's things, and one shirt hung inside out","Arvel","My wife done laundry thirty years, she says you hang a dark shirt inside out so it don't fade - so somebody knew what they was doing","June","That does sound like somebody keeping house","Arvel","There was eleven clothespins in the bag on the post - I counted 'em, I don't know why I counted 'em","Arvel","And then a dog started up somewhere behind the house and we left - so we left"}},
{"r8_hor_cake_no_flies","caller_story_horror",7,80,0,4,1,{"Dorsey","Kitchen of a house in Riverside, there's a cake on the counter under one of them glass covers","June","A birthday cake?","Dorsey","Candles stuck in it, eight of 'em, never lit, the wicks are still white - Icing's wrote on, I ain't going to say the name","June","That's all right","Dorsey","Cover's off, set beside it on the counter, right side up, and it's ninety-some degrees in that kitchen, been that way a month","Dorsey","There's not a fly on it - not one, there's flies on everything else in Knox County","June","I don't know what to make of that","Dorsey","Neither do I and I been a meat cutter twenty years - flies find it, that's the one thing about flies"}},
{"r8_hor_prints_one_direction","caller_story_horror",7,90,1,5,1,{"Ferrell","Boot prints across my garden every morning, same boots, waffle sole, big","June","Going which way?","Ferrell","Creek to the road, every morning, creek to the road, right through the beans","Ferrell","Never a print going back to the creek, not one, and that's soft ground, you can't cross it without leaving a mark","June","So he's coming out of the creek bottom and going up the road","Ferrell","Every day for nine days - a man's got to come back sometime, don't he? A man's got to sleep somewhere","June","Are you sleeping?","Ferrell","Some, my wife sits up the second half, we don't talk about it in front of the boy","Ferrell","I put a hoe by the back door, which ain't a plan - I know it ain't a plan"}},
{"r8_hor_voice_from_the_water","caller_story_horror",7,90,0,4,2,{"Lonnie","I'm camped down on the creek, me and my boy and my brother's family","June","How many of you?","Lonnie","Six, two tents and a tarp off the truck - we been down there since the water quit up top","Lonnie","Last night I heard my boy call me, from the water","Lonnie","He's asleep in the tent, he is asleep in the tent, I went and put my hand on him","June","He's with you right now","Lonnie","He's right here, he's eight years old and he's asleep and I have got my hand on his back this minute","June","Then that's what's true - stay where you are till it's light","Lonnie","It said Daddy twice, same as him - I ain't going down to that water again after dark, I don't care what we need"}},
{"r8_hor_note_says_we_know","caller_story_horror",7,90,23,5,2,{"June","You're on ninety-nine six","Junior","We leave notes at the Sav Rite - everybody does, taped inside the door glass, where you'd be","June","So people can find each other","Junior","Yeah, I put one up Monday, said the Cobb family, white house past the second cattle gate, knock and holler","Junior","Went back Wednesday for salt","June","Was the note still there?","Junior","Still there, somebody wrote under it - two words - we know","June","Under your note","Junior","Under it - pencil, neat little letters, and we moved Thursday, all six of us, and I ain't taping up nothing ever again"}},
{"exp_father_apron","caller_story_sad",8,3650,0,23,1,{"Della","Daddy had an apron for grilling, said he was head chef","June","Was he any good at it?","Della","Burned everything, we weren't allowed to call it burning","June","What were you supposed to call it?","Della","Extra flavor, the man could ruin a hot dog and make a speech about it","Della","I laughed about it this morning, then felt rotten for laughing","June","Sounds like he'd put some work into earning that laugh","Della","He'd have taken a bow, apron and all"}},
{"exp_uncle_plant","caller_joke",8,3650,0,23,1,{"Neal","My uncle left me in charge of his houseplant once","June","I suspect this ends badly for the plant","Neal","It was plastic, I watered it for three weeks","June","Did your uncle explain that when he got back?","Neal","He said it had never looked healthier","June","A tactful man","Neal","Made me promise to look after the lawn next","June","You checked whether that was real first, I hope"}},
{"exp_prison_freedom","caller_story_sad",8,3650,0,23,1,{"Vic","I used to know exactly what I'd do the first day I got out","June","You don't have to tell us where you were","Vic","Wasn't going to, I'd order breakfast someplace with a menu","June","Anything particular on the menu?","Vic","Didn't matter, wanted to be asked instead of handed a tray","June","Having a choice can mean a lot","Vic","Got out, didn't get the breakfast","Vic","Been trying to decide which part counts as freedom"}},
{"exp_lineman_porcelain","caller_story_sad",8,3650,0,23,1,{"Roy","People thought fixing power meant pulling a switch","Mack","A switch in a warm office, preferably","Roy","Never pictured us waiting beside a muddy ditch","Mack","You complained enough for them to hear","Roy","I liked the moment the windows lit up afterward","Mack","Didn't know you were sentimental about the work","Roy","I'm sentimental about getting a whole job finished","Mack","Keep that thought, we'll need it if we ever get a normal job again"}},
{"exp_appliance_noise","caller_joke",8,3650,0,23,1,{"Gil","I repaired appliances, every customer said it only made the noise when I wasn't there","June","And was that usually true?","Gil","Half the time, other half they'd unplugged it","June","That does cut down on noise","Gil","One fellow offered to record it on a cassette","June","Did that help?","Gil","He recorded his thumb over the microphone for twelve minutes","June","A very intimate portrait of the repair process"}},
{"king_radio_quiet_argument","caller_story_sad",8,3650,0,23,1,{"Nora","We had an argument over nothing","June","Did you sort it out?","Nora","I said sorry. He said he wasn't angry","June","Was he?","Nora","Probably. I would be","June","You could ask again when you've both had a minute","Nora","I keep thinking every argument has to be the last one","June","Maybe this one can just be an argument"}},
{"king_radio_bad_singing","caller_joke",8,3650,0,23,1,{"Bea","People keep asking me to sing something","June","Are you going to?","Bea","No. I'm protecting what little morale we have","June","That bad?","Bea","My brother used to offer me money to stop","June","Did you take it?","Bea","Of course. I knew my audience","June","Sounds like a sensible arrangement"}},
{"king_radio_phone_book","caller_joke",8,3650,0,23,1,{"Burt","Been reading the phone book. Not much of a plot","June","Lots of characters","Burt","Keep getting them mixed up","June","Any favorites?","Burt","Guy called A. A. Aaron. Knew how to get himself noticed","June","You going to finish it?","Burt","Don't ruin the ending for me","June","Wouldn't dream of it"}},
{"king_radio_dog_bowl","caller_story_sad",8,3650,0,23,1,{"Anne","I took the dog's bowl when I left. Didn't take much else","June","Was he with you?","Anne","No. Gate was open. I called till somebody made me stop","June","I'm sorry, Anne","Anne","Might sound stupid, carrying a bowl","June","Not to me","Anne","I keep thinking he won't recognize any of this if he finds me","June","He'd recognize you"}},
{"knox_birthday_candle","caller_story_sad",8,3650,0,23,1,{"Ruth","It was my birthday yesterday, I told nobody until today","June","Happy birthday, Ruth, late still counts","Ruth","Had a cracker with a match stuck in it, didn't light it - felt wasteful","June","You should have had a cake, I'm glad you got another day"}},
{"knox_empty_air","silence",8,3650,0,5,1,{"June","I'm leaving a little quiet now","June","Not every gap means the equipment's gone","June","Sometimes somebody's gathering the nerve to press the button","June","Take your time, I'll stop talking"}},
{"knox_coffee_review","caller_joke",8,3650,0,23,1,{"Art","Made coffee so bad I apologized to the cup","June","Was the cup understanding?","Art","It was chipped, been through worse","June","Haven't we all, Art, haven't we all"}},
{"knox_supervisor","caller_joke",8,3650,0,23,1,{"Cal","Good news, I haven't heard from my supervisor in weeks","June","Cal, that's not necessarily good news","Cal","No, but I bet he's still writing me up for attendance somewhere","June","If he calls this station, I'm telling him you're on lunch"}},
{"knox_obit_seamstress","obituary",8,3650,0,23,1,{"Mabel","I'd like to say something for my sister Ellen, she sewed everybody's hems for nothing","June","Go ahead, Mabel","Mabel","She'd complain the entire time, made sure you knew what a nuisance you were","Mabel","Then she'd fix the pocket you hadn't even mentioned, that's who she was"}},
{"knox_last_message","caller_story_sad",8,3650,0,23,1,{"Ben","Last thing I said to my brother was that he owed me twenty dollars","June","It wasn't the only thing you ever said to him","Ben","I know, wish my head would let the other things have a turn","June","Tell us one of those, if you want, we have time"}},
{"knox_no_rescue_claim","instruction",8,3650,0,23,1,{"June","A reminder, a voice on a radio is not a rescue team","June","That includes mine, I can't see your street, and I can't promise somebody is coming","June","I'm sorry if that's not the thing you needed to hear","June","I'd rather disappoint you than have you waiting at a door for a promise I couldn't keep"}},
{"knox_trade_boundary","trade",8,3650,0,23,1,{"June","People have asked to arrange trades through this station","June","I can't verify what anyone owns, and I'm not guaranteeing a meeting","June","Don't confuse someone sounding friendly with someone you know","June","If that sounds suspicious, well, I'd like you around to complain about it tomorrow"}},
{"knox_footsteps_memory","caller_story_horror",8,3650,0,23,1,{"Len","For two nights I thought somebody was pacing upstairs","June","Did you ever find out?","Len","Loose shutter outside, wind was knocking it against the wall, I checked in daylight","Len","Didn't stop me hearing footsteps the third night, that's the part I hate"}},
{"knox_sign_on_survivors","sign_on",8,3650,0,23,1,{"June","This is June, back at the microphone","June","No theme music - no sponsors, very questionable management","June","We're still not an official service, and I still won't pretend to know what I don't","June","But if you needed proof somebody else can speak today, hello"}},
{"r2_d8_net_call_nguyen","military",8,11,5,9,1,{"Warden Tac","All Warden stations, this is Warden Tac, net call, report in order, over","Warden Tac","Anvil, over","Anvil-7","Anvil-7 for Anvil-6 - Anvil-6 is out of action, thirty-one present, over","Warden Tac","Roger, Anvil - Hatchet, over","Warden Tac","Hatchet, Hatchet, Warden Tac, over","Hatchet-6","Hatchet-6, sorry, Tac, I was out on the wire - Hatchet present, strength follows by runner, over","Warden Tac","Roger - Crowbar, over","Warden Tac","Crowbar, Crowbar, this is Warden Tac, radio check, over","Warden Tac","Striker, over","Striker-7","Striker-7 - Striker-6 says present - Tac, who's running this net, over?","Warden Tac","Specialist Nguyen, over","Striker-7","Where's the battle captain, over?","Warden Tac","Asleep, Sergeant, first time since a week ago Friday - I told him I'd run the net - Warden Tac, out"}},
{"r3_so_d8_week_two","sign_on",8,9,5,8,1,{"Marty","Good morning, Knox County, ninety-nine point six, March Ridge, this is Marty Colburn, starting in on week two","Marty","A man who stopped in for dog food told me I sound less like a hostage than I did last week - I've decided to take that kindly","Marty","It's {time}, the generator's running on diesel a young man from Rosewood siphoned out of a school bus and hauled over in milk jugs","Marty","He traded it for four sacks of chicken feed and a promise that I'd say hello to his mother on the air","Marty","So, hello, Mrs. Dotson, your boy says eat something","Marty","Scanner notes after this, and then the names"}},
{"r3_wx_d8_wring_it_out","weather",8,15,5,10,1,{"Marty","Weather for {weekday}, hot, then hotter - ninety-four by the thermometer on the grain bin this afternoon, and a heat index the television used to call dangerous, back when it had anything to call","Marty","Humidity you could wring out of the air with your two hands","Marty","Nothing in the rain gauge in five days, if your garden's still alive, water at dusk, at the roots, not on the leaves","Marty","A little breeze out of the southwest after dinner, it won't help, but it'll feel like it's trying","Marty","Dee wants me to add, drink water before you're thirsty - I've been told to say it twice - drink water before you're thirsty"}},
{"r5_obit_marty_quarters_homer","obituary",8,20,6,21,2,{"Marty","The station in Elizabethtown used to read the death notices right after the farm report - nobody's reading them now, so I'm going to","Marty","I only read what folks bring me or call in, no guessing - if I get one wrong, tell me and I'll correct it on the air","Marty","Homer Ledbetter, seventy-one, of March Ridge, he bought feed at my store for thirty years and paid cash every time","Marty","And every time, he'd leave a quarter on the counter and say, 'That's for the cat'","Marty","I never had a cat, I told him so for thirty years - he left the quarter anyway","Marty","There's a coffee can under my register with, I'd guess, three hundred dollars in quarters in it - I don't know what to do with it, I'm keeping it"}},
{"r7_fire_station_33_last_run","scanner",8,14,6,22,1,{"Engine 33","Anybody on this channel, Engine 33 out of Station 33 - this is the last run we've got diesel for","Engine 33","We're at the Kelso place with a load of water and we're going to fill everything they hold out - jugs, tubs, a hog trough, whatever's clean","Engine 33","Then we're taking this truck to Little Bethel and doing the same thing there, and then she's parked with the tank full","Engine 33","There'll be eighteen hundred gallons sitting in the bay at Station 33 with the door unlocked - somebody's gonna need it in January","Engine 33","Bay door lifts by hand if you get two men on it - don't fool with the pump, just open the tank valve at the back step","Engine 33","That's Engine 33 and that's Otto and me - show us out of service, ain't nobody left to show us to, but show us out anyway"}},
{"r7_ems_last_rig_running","scanner",8,14,0,23,1,{"EMS 1","Any station on this channel, EMS 1, I'm the only unit in service in this county and I've been the only one since the weekend","EMS 1","I've got fuel for maybe two days of running and I've got no oxygen, no morphine, and about a case and a half of bandages","EMS 1","So here's how it works now, I come for children, and I come for bleeding, and I come for a woman having a baby","EMS 1","I don't come for a fever and I don't come for a bite - if that's you, I'm sorry, and I'll say it to your face if you want me to","EMS 1","If you can drive, drive, if you can carry, carry, if you know how to stop a bleed, teach the person next to you tonight","EMS 1","EMS 1 is 10-8 and I sleep in the truck at the fire hall on 31W - bang on the door, I'll wake up, I always wake up"}},
{"r8_hor_christmas_lights_july","caller_story_horror",8,120,22,4,2,{"Glenda","Am I on? Sorry, I had to move the antenna off the gutter","June","You're on - go ahead","Glenda","There's a porch out past the second cattle gate on Echo Creek with Christmas lights strung on it - blinking","Glenda","It's nowhere near Christmas, poles are down at that curve, have been since the sixth - ain't a wire hot for two mile","June","You're certain they were lit","Glenda","I set in the road and watched 'em go around - blue, blue, white, around and around and around","Glenda","My husband says battery - Mister fix-it, he wouldn't get out of the truck neither, so","June","Then I'll leave it as lights on a porch","Glenda","That's all I want anybody to do with it, I just needed it said out loud by somebody besides me"}},
{"r8_hor_mail_sorted_floor","caller_story_horror",8,90,21,3,1,{"Dee","Marty's asleep in the chair so you're getting me - go ahead, you're on ninety-nine six","Loyd","Post office in Ekron - back room, where the carriers work up the routes","Loyd","Mail's all over the floor, which, sure, kicked around, folks been through it looking for checks","Loyd","But there's four stacks on the floor by the wall, squared up, rubber banded - sorted by street","Dee","Sorted since all this?","Loyd","There's a letter on top with an August postmark on it - August - so yeah - since","Dee","Somebody's still working the route","Loyd","Somebody's still working the route, and I'd like to know which house they think they're carrying it to"}},
{"r8_hor_phone_books_same_page","caller_story_horror",8,100,22,4,1,{"Alma","This is going to sound like I'm crazy and you can say so","June","I'm not going to say that","Alma","Every phone book I've picked up in two weeks is laid open to the same page - the S's","Alma","Four houses, the payphone stand out front of the Sav Rite, the one hanging on a chain at the feed store","June","Open to the same page","Alma","Same page, not the same spot on the page, I checked that, it ain't a crease - they're just open at the S's","June","You looked at the names","Alma","I looked - Stinson, Sparks, Six, Stiles, regular county names - ours is in there too, and I wish it wasn't"}},
{"r8_hor_whistling_last_note","caller_story_horror",8,100,23,5,1,{"Chester","Somebody whistling out by the road at night - same tune","June","A song you know?","Chester","An old one - church one, my mother whistled it doing dishes, I couldn't tell you the name of it","Chester","He gets to the last note and he don't whistle it - stops right there - every time","June","Every time","Chester","Six or seven times a night, gets right up to it and quits, and starts the whole thing over","Chester","You ever have a song stop one note short? Your head finishes it for you - your head can't help it","June","That's a hard thing to lie there under","Chester","I've took to humming it out loud to finish it - my daughter caught me at it and asked was I all right, and I said sure, hon"}},
{"r8_hor_screen_door_no_door","caller_story_horror",8,100,22,4,1,{"Marvis","Our screen door got tore off in the first week - a fella backed a truck into it, long story, he's dead now","June","Go on","Marvis","There's a hole in the frame and a piece of plywood screwed over the opening - no door, nothing to swing","Marvis","And I hear it, that slap it makes - you know the sound, the spring pulls it to and it hits twice, bap, bap","June","From that doorway?","Marvis","From that doorway, six, eight times a night, like people coming in and out of a house on a Sunday","June","Is the plywood still on it in the morning?","Marvis","Still on, same four screws, I marked 'em with a pencil and they ain't turned","Marvis","So there's a door there that ain't there and folks are coming and going through it - I don't know what else to tell you"}},
{"r8_hor_says_my_words_back","caller_story_horror",8,100,1,5,1,{"Opal","Whatever I said, he'd say the end of it back to me - quiet, under his breath","June","Repeating you","Opal","I'd say the road's washed out past the bridge, and he'd go, past the bridge - just like that, soft, looking at the ground","June","Like he was remembering it","Opal","Like he was learning it, there's a difference and I can't put it in words for you but there's a difference","Opal","I quit talking after a while, just to see, and he stood there and didn't say nothing at all","June","For how long?","Opal","Long enough that I said something just to fill it - and he said the end of that too","Opal","I sent him on with a can of corn, I hope he's all right, I do hope that - I just hope it's somewhere else"}},
{"r8_hor_twelve_empty_runs","caller_story_horror",8,100,22,4,1,{"Merle","Kennel out on Tanner Road - Boarding place, the lady kept dogs while folks was on vacation","June","I know it","Merle","Twelve runs, chain link, concrete floors, gates on 'em - we went for the feed, there's usually feed at a kennel","Merle","Every gate stood open - no dogs","June","Somebody turned them loose","Merle","That's what a decent person does, and I'd have done it - but there's no mess in them runs, not a bit - Concrete's clean","Merle","Twelve dogs penned up with nobody to hose 'em down - there ought to be a smell you can't stand in - there wasn't nothing","June","Nothing at all","Merle","Water buckets full, feed in the barrel - twelve open gates, I'm about done going in places where somebody was good to the animals"}},
{"r8_hor_buck_wont_look","caller_story_horror",8,100,22,4,2,{"June","Line's open, go ahead","Hoyt","My dog won't look at the tree line","June","Won't look at it","Hoyt","Buck, eight year old walker hound, best nose in three counties, and he has never been afraid of anything in his life - he's treed a bear","Hoyt","He'll look at me, he'll look at the fire - he'll look at the truck, the gate, a bird","Hoyt","He will not look at them trees, he turns his whole head off to the side to get around 'em","June","Since when?","Hoyt","Wednesday evening, he come in off the field at a walk, not a run, and he laid down under the porch and he ain't been out from under it since","June","And he won't go out","Hoyt","I've called him, I don't call him twice, that ain't fair to a dog - so that's why we don't cut firewood in that timber no more"}},
{"r8_hor_headlights_none_arrive","caller_story_horror",8,105,1,5,1,{"Loyd","Headlights on 31W at two in the morning, strung out, a dozen sets maybe, all headed north","June","People moving at night","Loyd","Sure, that's the smart hour to move, and I'd not blame a soul for it","Loyd","My place is on that road, you go by my mailbox, I hear you - I've heard every car on that road for nineteen years","June","And you didn't hear them","Loyd","Not one, watched 'em go up the valley for twenty minutes, one set after another, and there was no engines and nothing come past the box","June","Nothing arrived","Loyd","There's five miles of that road I can see from the porch and they was on the far end of it the whole time","Loyd","My son says weather, lights bending over the hill, he's a smart boy - then it's the weather, I've quit sitting on that side of the porch anyhow"}},
{"r9_trade_d8_tools_she_cant_look_at","trade",8,40,9,16,1,{"Marty","First note out of the slot this morning isn't a trade - I'm going to read it as one anyhow, because that's how she asked me to do it","Caller - Dovie","I've got my husband's tools, all of them - the rollaway box, the sockets, the good level, the come-along - I want them gone out of here","Marty","And you want what for them, Miz Dovie?","Caller - Dovie","Nothing, I don't need a thing - I need them out of the garage because I have to walk through the garage to get to the freezer","Marty","I can't read a giveaway or folks will swarm you - how about this instead, you tell me what you're keeping, first, out loud","Caller - Dovie","I'm keeping the tape measure, he scratched his name in it in seventy-nine so nobody at the plant would walk off with it","Marty","Then here's the trade, one tool to a family, and you bring her something to eat when you come, whatever you've got in the house - the place with the pump house on Tanner Road, knock and step back off the door"}},
{"king_radio_teaching_whistle","caller_story_sad",9,3650,0,23,1,{"Mae","I tried teaching someone to whistle","June","How did that go?","Mae","Badly. Mostly air and accusations","June","I never could do it either","Mae","He said my instructions were terrible","June","Were they?","Mae","Absolutely. We were happy for about ten minutes","June","Ten minutes counts"}},
{"king_radio_shop_credit","caller_story_sad",9,3650,0,23,1,{"Lois","I used to keep a little book of what people owed at the shop","June","Did people pay?","Lois","Mostly. Some took longer. We didn't put their names up anywhere","June","What happened to the book?","Lois","Left it on the counter. Couldn't think why I'd carry it","June","Makes sense","Lois","Wish I'd kept the messages in the margins, though. They weren't all debts","June","What do you remember?"}},
{"king_radio_mechanic_habit","caller_joke",9,3650,0,23,1,{"Roy","Caught myself wiping my hands before I answered the radio","June","Don't want to get it dirty?","Roy","Used to do it for customers. Habit, I guess","June","You can take your time","Roy","Want me to tell you it'll be ready Friday?","June","Would it be?","Roy","Not a chance","June","You're an honest mechanic, Roy"}},
{"r2_d9_dee_explains_refusal","military",9,13,18,23,2,{"Marty","I have company at the microphone tonight - Deanna Price, night nurse from Muldraugh, she walked into my store Thursday and asked if the radio man wanted his blood pressure checked","Dee","He did, it was terrible, hi, everybody, I'm Dee - I'm going to help Marty with the Army traffic, because a lot of it turns out to be medical","Marty","Last week we played you a helicopter turning down a soldier with a cut arm - a lot of you asked me why, I didn't have an answer","Dee","Here's the why, plainly, their rule was no flight for anybody hurt by one of those things - a scratch counts, nobody wants a sick man inside a hospital full of people who can't run","Dee","I'm not saying it was right, I'm saying I've stood at an emergency room door and made that call about who comes inside - it doesn't make you a monster, it makes you the one at the door","Marty","Did you ever hear what happened to him? The specialist?","Dee","No, but the surgeon had the medic write the temperature on the back of his hand - that's a good trick - write it where it can't get lost","Dee","If you're nursing somebody at home, do that, pen on the hand, every hour, if the numbers climb past a hundred and two, you make your plans"}},
{"r3_so_d9_dee_arrives","sign_on",9,9,5,8,6,{"Marty","Good morning, it's {weekday}, {date}, before anything else, there's somebody here I want you to meet","Marty","She walked into my lot at about four this morning carrying a backpack and a transistor radio, and asked if I was the fellow who can't pronounce Muldraugh","Marty","I pronounce it fine - go ahead and introduce yourself","Dee","Hi, I'm Deanna Price - Dee, I was a night nurse in Muldraugh for eleven years, and he does not pronounce it fine","Marty","Dee has offered to take the late hours, and to answer the medical questions I've been making up answers to","Dee","Which, for the record, were mostly okay - mostly","Marty","I'll take mostly - it's {time}, this is ninety-nine point six"}},
{"r3_sf_d9_dee_first_night","sign_off",9,10,23,2,4,{"Dee","This is Dee - Marty's gone to bed, if you can call a cot next to the fertilizer a bed","Dee","I'm used to being awake right now, eleven years of nights - my body thinks it's time for two o'clock vitals","Dee","So here's how nights are going to go, the broadcast ends now to save fuel - but I'll be sitting up with the CB on nineteen","Dee","If you're awake with a sick kid or a bad feeling, key up - I can't come to you, but I can stay up with you, and staying up is the thing I'm best at","Dee","This is Dee Price, ninety-nine point six is off the air"}},
{"r3_host_d9_room_fourteen","host",9,12,0,23,4,{"Marty","Dee, folks are going to want to know how you found us","Dee","One of my residents had a little transistor radio - Mrs. Beulah Carter, room fourteen, she kept it on the nightstand for the ball games","Dee","Sunday night I was sitting with her, turning the dial for anything at all, and there was this man reading instructions about bathtubs like he was reading a feed order","Marty","That would be me","Dee","Beulah said, 'That man sounds scared to death.' And I said yes ma'am - and she said, 'Well, somebody ought to go help him'","Dee","I stayed with her through Thursday, then I brought the radio","Marty","It's sitting right here on the desk","Dee","There's a strip of tape on the back with her name on it, so it wouldn't get mixed up with anybody else's - room fourteen"}},
{"r3_ins_d9_salt_sugar_quart","instruction",9,30,5,12,4,{"Dee","This is Dee, everybody listen, because I'm going to say this about once a day for the rest of my life","Dee","Bad water gives you diarrhea, diarrhea in this heat will kill you faster than those things will, and it's a lot less dignified","Dee","Here's the fix, one quart of clean water - six level teaspoons of sugar, half a level teaspoon of salt - Stir it till it's gone","Dee","Sip it - don't gulp it, a child gets a spoonful every minute or two, even if some comes back up - keep going","Dee","No measuring spoons? It should taste no saltier than tears - that's how the old nurses taught it, six sugar, half salt, one quart"}},
{"r4_sad_dee_chili_message","caller_story_sad",9,30,18,23,2,{"Dee","Marty, I need the microphone for a minute, I've got a message I promised to deliver and I've been carrying it around for over a week","Marty","It's yours","Dee","Friday night, the ninth, a man came into the clinic in Muldraugh - bitten on the forearm, he knew what it meant before I did","Dee","His name was Carl - Carl Whitt, he was polite - he apologized for bleeding on my floor, he asked me to call his wife","Dee","I said I would, phones were already going - I never got through","Dee","So - Linda Whitt, this is Deanna, the night nurse - Carl wanted me to tell you the chili is in the deep freeze - bottom left, under the peas","Dee","And he said don't let your brother have any of it, because he'll just say it needs more salt","Dee","That was it, that's what he picked, I asked him if there was anything else and he said no ma'am, she'll know","Marty","(Marty doesn't say anything - Dee doesn't either, the carrier runs on for a while)","Dee","Okay, delivered"}},
{"r4_sad_glove_under_mattress","caller_story_sad",9,30,18,22,1,{"Caller - Annette","My son bought a new ball glove with his mowing money - real leather, he was so serious about breaking it in","Caller - Annette","He oiled it, put a baseball in the pocket, wrapped it with two of my hair ties, and put it under his mattress - Thursday night the eighth","Caller - Annette","He said you have to sleep on it two weeks or the pocket won't set right - his coach told him that, it was law","Dee","Two weeks is a long time when you're twelve","Caller - Annette","It's been two weeks, it's been more than two weeks","Caller - Annette","I made his bed today and I felt the lump of it under there - I put my hand on it through the mattress","Caller - Annette","I'm not taking the ball out, it's not done yet - he'd be so mad if I took it out before it was set","Dee","(Dee starts to speak, and doesn't)","Marty","(Marty reaches over and turns the station fan off, so there's no noise at all)"}},
{"r4_sad_hearing_aid_loud","caller_story_sad",9,30,10,21,1,{"Caller - Floyd","I'm sorry if I'm too loud - tell me if I'm too loud, I've got a habit","Marty","You're fine, sir - go on","Caller - Floyd","Wife was hard of hearing thirty years, hearing aids, both ears - you had to talk up, whole house talked loud, the dog barked loud","Caller - Floyd","She kept those little batteries in the refrigerator door, in the egg tray - said it made them last","Caller - Floyd","Fridge has been off since the power went, I still keep them in there - still in the egg tray, nothing else in there to speak of","Caller - Floyd","And I still talk loud, in the empty house, I say good morning like I'm calling across a parking lot","Caller - Floyd","Tried to talk regular yesterday - quiet, didn't sound like the house at all - sounded like somebody else's house","Dee","You go right on talking loud, Floyd","Caller - Floyd","WHAT? Heh, that was her joke - that was hers","Marty","(The laugh stops, neither host picks the moment back up - they let it sit)"}},
{"r4_sad_camp_letter_indiana","caller_story_sad",9,30,17,22,1,{"Caller - Lisa","The last day the mail ran, there was a letter in the box from my son - he's at church camp in southern Indiana, across the river","Dee","Across the river, outside all of this","Caller - Lisa","Postmarked the eighth, it says, Dear Mom, the food is gross, a boy named Tyler snores, please send drink mix, the grape kind","Caller - Lisa","Camp was supposed to end on the seventeenth, I was supposed to pick him up in the church parking lot","Caller - Lisa","So he's out there, he's the one who got out - he's the lucky one in this family, and he's eleven, and he doesn't know where we are","Caller - Lisa","I've got four packets of grape in the kitchen drawer - I bought them to mail him and I didn't get to the post office","Caller - Lisa","If this signal gets across the river at all - Jason Moore - Mom got your letter, the grape kind, I've got it right here","Marty","(Marty says nothing for a long moment)","Dee","We'll say that one again tomorrow, Lisa, and the day after"}},
}
